WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.980
<b>A Giant Leap</b>

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.990
Akira!

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.270
You guys.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.010
My dear!

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.220
I'm so glad you're all okay.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.010
Alma, what happened with Soma?

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.210
I... killed him.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.090
Sorry, Alma. 
I put you in a really difficult situation.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:40.220
No, the one taking it the hardest is...

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.850
Forgive me, Minami.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:44.810
It's okay.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.780
I know you both did everything you could.

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:50.800
Thank you.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.060
But... I wish I could've helped him!

00:00:56.020 --> 00:01:00.740
I had no idea he was suffering so much!

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:04.180
Sorry, Soma...

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:06.200
I'm so sorry!

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.700
I'm sorry... So sorry!

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:14.550
Minami.

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:19.720
Yo, looks like the geezer managed to survive.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.310
Kondo.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:24.830
What was that Beta thing, though?

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:27.020
Did Auctioneer know anything?

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.490
Well...

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:33.260
Hang on. Tell me one last thing before I go.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:35.800
What exactly is Beta?

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.080
How did I end up becoming Number 00?

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:45.250
The only person likely to have
those answers is Doctor Iriya.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.310
But isn't he long dead?

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:55.710
No. He's still alive, 
just in a different form.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:58.900
I was working in collaboration with him.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.110
We're out of time.

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:08.310
Just know that Doctor Iriya will show himself 
before you sooner rather than later.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.400
Doctor Iriya... is alive?

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.960
No way.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:16.360
He can't be.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.430
Is that true?

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:22.220
Mama Kaori!

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:23.320
CEO.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.050
Wait, so you are...

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:31.420
Yes. Munakata Kaori, 
CEO of Iriya Heavy Industries.

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:34.860
Do you know everything, then?

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:39.620
No, only Doctor Iriya does.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:43.440
What the...?

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:44.600
An explosion?

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:47.060
It's coming from Kasumigaseki!

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.810
Fighter jets?

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:55.730
They're turning around and coming this way!

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:58.110
They're aiming for this building, Akira!

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.530
Get down, you guys!

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.020
You all okay?!

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.540
<i>Do you hear me, Akira?!</i>

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:16.840
Chikage?

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:18.520
I'm glad you're all right.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:20.620
<i>What is going on?</i>

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:24.640
We don't have much of a clue either, 
but it seems we've been hacked.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:28.020
They're attacking Japan's political centers!

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.810
<i>I'm afraid I have even more bad news.</i>

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:40.430
Bombers had been deployed, 
in case we couldn't put Beta down,

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:43.210
and Chief Shiga, 
who was in one of them, has died.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:53.040
What? Even the chief?

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:12.120
Disaster Response! 
Munakata here, give me a sitrep.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.960
<i>The whole building might go down! 
Evacuate at once!</i>

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:16.880
The emergency staircase seems fine!

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:17.770
Got it!

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.800
What the hell is all this?

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.340
It's a scene out of hell.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:36.310
This is a terrorist attack 
involving large-scale hacking.

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:38.960
Wait. We took out Beta, didn't we?

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.420
That much is for sure.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:45.740
Number 11's black hole sucked in 
his brain for sure.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:48.960
So what, we're dealing with
Gamma now? Or Delta?

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.860
This is absurd!

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:53.790
Anyway, I'll go online 
and look for the perp.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:54.760
Akira?

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:57.730
What? Why do I feel so sluggish?

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.250
You're at your limit.

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:03.570
If you strain yourself
any further, you'll die.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:04.940
No!

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:07.930
I don't care. Let me go.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.320
I can't afford to stop now.

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:21.820
Actually, it's not about 
what I can or can't do.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.180
I want to keep going!

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:28.800
Akira...

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:33.860
Minami, remember what you said 
back when we first met?

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:40.110
The strong must use their powers 
to protect the weak!

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:48.990
With Ogre and the EX-ARMs, I'm a monster. 
The strongest in the world.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:55.980
So I'm going to fight for the weak, 
just as you taught me to.

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:58.310
Akira!

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:03.880
Protect the world, please.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.970
You got it!

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:13.390
<i>Heading to the building's basement!</i>

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:14.390
Copy that!

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.460
Doctor Iriya is alive?

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:22.120
Doctor Iriya is alive.

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:25.850
Doctor Iriya is...

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:36.660
Now, I suppose I'll take a front-row seat 
and see how my experiment plays out.

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:40.660
Where are you going, Doctor?

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:46.420
This is it. The basement.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:49.240
Are you ready?

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:53.820
My dear, I will support you with all I have.

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:55.630
I'll be with you, too.

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:56.600
Thanks.

00:06:57.030 --> 00:06:59.160
Look at this kid, acting all cool.

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:01.760
You better come back to us, Akira.

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:02.690
Gotcha!

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:08.570
Be careful, Alma. And take care of Akira.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:10.700
Okay, Minami.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:25.460
Unlocking all my dear's networking capabilities.

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:32.840
All of Tokyo, save for Iriya HQ, 
is being taken over by the enemy.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:35.720
All the infrastructure and public transport 
is out of control, too.

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:38.460
Leave the real world to us.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:41.010
We'll keep things safe, no matter what.

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:42.430
Counting on ya.

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:43.730
Let's go, Ygg.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:46.420
Okay! Initializing connection!

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:53.280
What is that?

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:55.280
An enemy attack program.

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:04.000
I'll layer real-time footage 
from the outside to our vision.

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:16.440
Is this the state of Tokyo's network right now?

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.970
Hey, that car's being attacked by some monster!

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.310
That's the visualization of the attack command.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:24.730
I'll go.

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:30.440
I see now.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:34.350
If we take them out, 
we can stop all the chaos happening out there.

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:37.310
There's too many of them, though.

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:38.830
That storm...

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:40.990
That's where the hack's originating from.

00:08:40.990 --> 00:08:42.080
We need to take it out.

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:43.920
Okay, I'll handle that.

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:46.630
You two focus on saving 
as many people as you can.

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.000
Akira?

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:50.260
Take her with you.

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:52.010
Okay. Take care of things.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:56.660
Alma, we'll clean all this up 
with parallel processing.

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:57.390
Okay.

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:06.280
No...

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:10.190
This is Ichigaya. Has the Japanese military's 
main server been taken over?

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:15.340
Ygg, what are those?

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:17.200
Beta... or not.

00:09:17.630 --> 00:09:20.680
Their algorithms are similar 
to Beta's thought process,

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:23.290
but there are various other things mixed in.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:27.850
It seems Akira made it to the main server.

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:30.160
Boss! The building's not gonna hold!

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:31.870
Have all the staff evacuated?

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.840
No, more than half are still in here.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:34.720
What?

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:38.110
Guess we have a job to do.

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:39.610
We'll go lead the evac.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:42.780
Can't let Akira steal all the spotlight.

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:45.140
I'd appreciate that.

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:48.570
<i>Nothing's working! We're gonna crash!</i>

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:54.900
<i>Controls back online! Correcting elevation!</i>

00:09:56.240 --> 00:10:00.910
We'll keep casualties to a minimum. 
Hurry up, Akira.

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:05.440
And we'll keep things safe here as promised.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:08.540
So don't give up, Akira.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:14.130
Alisa? Weren't you in HQ?

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:21.850
Wait, no. You are...?

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:24.830
Did you enjoy my Oscar-worthy performance?

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:27.980
I even modified my own memories 
to get into the act.

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:30.790
Who exactly are you?

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:35.910
Isn't identifying the enemy 
a more pressing matter?

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:41.110
I can tell you what it is Natsume
Akira is fighting.

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:44.990
<b>Illustration by Komi Shinya</b>

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.860
Ugh! There's no end to them!

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:55.790
The enemy's launching attacks 
on networks worldwide

00:10:55.790 --> 00:10:58.090
and adding them to its arsenal as we speak.

00:10:58.090 --> 00:10:59.050
What?

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:03.290
Those monsters are virtual manifestations 
of corrupted servers.

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:07.880
As they expand, their processing power will grow 
and make them more powerful.

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:13.060
Then we just gotta beat them down 
and bring them back, right?

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:16.700
The thing Natsume Akira's fighting is...

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:19.460
Wait, it's not still Beta, is it?

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:24.320
Beta itself vanished 
into Number 11's black hole.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:28.870
But there remained several AIs 
that had been corrupted by it.

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:31.690
You don't mean 
the Amaterasu multibots' AI, do you?

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:34.140
Bingo.

00:11:34.140 --> 00:11:40.710
The corrupted AIs were analyzed 
by the JDF's tactical computers in Ichigaya.

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:46.510
But when the analytical AI came in contact 
with Beta's malice and destructive urges,

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:49.740
they unlocked all the limiters placed on it.

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:53.990
It became a tactical AI 
with a will of its own.

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:59.670
That's the root cause of all this chaos.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:06.600
It's already infiltrating global networks, 
not just Japan's.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:08.220
Akira!

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:11.370
Bad news, my dear!

00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:15.880
ICBMs were just launched from military bases 
under the enemy's control.

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:18.500
Where are the missiles headed?

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:21.100
Their targets... are the entire planet.

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:22.550
What?!

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:25.640
The first one will hit its target 
in eleven minutes.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:28.270
Got it. I'll get rid of those missiles.

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:29.510
Help me out here.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:30.940
Sure!

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:33.380
Let's go!

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:40.700
This is the peak altitude 
of the ICBMs' trajectories.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:42.220
Look over there, Akira.

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:43.740
There they are.

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:45.360
What can we use?

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:53.660
Found something!

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:56.120
The Japanese military's laser satellite?

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:57.620
I'm using it!

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:01.130
Missiles getting closer!

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:03.050
Fire!

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.120
You did it!

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:12.670
No, not yet.

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:14.810
Weapons all over the world...

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:17.400
are going out of control!

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:24.970
All kinds of unmanned weapons 
across the globe are being activated.

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:28.910
Multibots, bombers, even ballistic missiles.

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:32.250
They've all been taken over by those monsters.

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:35.410
Dammit! What the hell are those things?

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.330
I've seen eyes like those before.

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:42.920
The outlaws we've encountered so far 
and their victims all had

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:47.320
the blank stare you get when you fall 
into the clutches of hatred and despair.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:52.640
So if I had it call it something...

00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:55.480
Human malice?

00:13:56.050 --> 00:13:57.360
Exactly.

00:13:57.360 --> 00:14:02.380
Those monsters are made of the tactical
programs installed on the main server

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:04.080
combined with a history of war...

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:07.020
Memories of mankind's fear and hatred.

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:09.640
It has taken the form 
of a species that prospers

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:13.800
by killing nature, animals, 
and even fellow humans.

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:17.040
You could call it 
the face of humanity itself.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:22.650
The EX-ARMs Natsume Akira possesses 
can amplify human desires,

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:26.260
and thus can also amplify malice.

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:30.120
No, you're forgetting something important.

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:34.780
If EX-ARMs can amplify human desires,

00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:39.100
then they can also amplify the virtues 
of mankind, and even its loving nature!

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:42.220
Maybe so.

00:14:42.220 --> 00:14:46.440
But the malice is a force 
to be reckoned with.

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:54.340
My dear?

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:59.370
You two should disconnect from the network. 
I'll handle the rest.

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:00.920
My dear?

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:02.880
Do you have a plan?

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.350
Nope.

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:11.950
I'll have to go after each and every one 
of the servers and weapons it's taken over.

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:15.440
I can't even afford the lag caused
by sharing information with you two.

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:17.400
I've gotta do this alone.

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:22.620
Understood. Then I shall shut down 
my persona interface.

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:27.780
Connect to my body directly 
and use it as an additional resource.

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:30.330
That should get rid of the lag.

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:31.450
Alma?

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:36.280
I don't mind offering you my everything.

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:40.800
Use me too, my dear.

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:44.250
You can have all of Yggdrasil's resources.

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:47.670
Wait, you two can't do that!

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:52.920
Mother, we were created to serve mankind.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:57.470
I believe now is the time 
to carry out our purpose.

00:15:57.960 --> 00:16:00.090
Please let them.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:03.050
You're back?

00:16:03.050 --> 00:16:05.440
We managed to get everyone out.

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:09.530
There's probably nothing we can do anymore.

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:12.440
I'll leave the future up to Akira and those two.

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:17.280
The world's in your hands, Akira, Alma, Ygg.

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:19.340
Sure.

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:25.710
I never could have children,

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:29.210
but I wonder if this is how it feels 
to marry off a daughter.

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:31.450
I understand.

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:38.540
Akira, I'll leave my two daughters 
and mankind's future to you!

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:41.050
Thank you.

00:16:43.490 --> 00:16:44.760
It's so pretty.

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:46.440
<b>let's do this</b>

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:46.980
Let's do this!

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:55.860
<i>The next hour or so was an extremely
strange time to experience.</i>

00:16:56.470 --> 00:17:00.870
<i>The final battle to decide 
the world's fate was underway,</i>

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:06.620
<i>something akin to the Armageddon 
or Ragnarok of legends,</i>

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:10.880
<i>but it was all just so quiet.</i>

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:22.460
<i>All anyone could do was watch helplessly 
as the world's fate hung in the balance.</i>

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:34.700
<i>The attacks in New York have stopped!</i>

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:36.750
<i>London, Hong Kong, Milan...</i>

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:40.140
<i>The unmanned attacks across the globe 
are being canceled!</i>

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:41.700
<i>That leaves only Japan!</i>

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:44.960
<i>Ogre's brain temperature is rising even further!</i>

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.150
Akira...

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:53.370
Damn it. But I'm almost done...

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:57.740
Well? What's your trump card?

00:17:57.740 --> 00:18:03.050
Human malice can't be erased so easily, hero.

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:09.810
This place won't last much longer! 
We gotta bounce!

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:15.150
Akira's limiting the enemy 
to basically just Japan.

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:17.700
We can't just leave him and run away.

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:21.080
Nah. You should go, Minami.

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:22.160
Akira?

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:27.370
Listen, I tried what I could, 
but I can't whittle them down any further.

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:32.470
And it looks like my gray cells 
have truly reached their limit.

00:18:34.610 --> 00:18:40.470
So I've decided to send a bunch of
nuclear missiles to the skies above Tokyo,

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:47.390
and detonate them above the stratosphere... 
at an altitude of over 100 km.

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:49.350
Wait, you don't mean...

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:53.480
An EMP attack using
high-altitude nuclear explosions?

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:57.670
Nuclear explosions at an altitude 
of 30 km to 400 km...

00:18:57.670 --> 00:19:00.080
...will make gamma rays collide 
with air molecules,

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:05.370
make them release their electrons, 
and cause EMP emissions within a radius of 100 km!

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:11.080
All of Japan's electronics will be destroyed, 
and all data will be lost.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:12.830
Including the enemy.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:18.260
But that might prove more damaging 
to Japan than the Tokyo Attack!

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:20.470
Yeah, I know.

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:24.390
EX-ARMs are nothing but a plague.

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:25.810
But...

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:29.130
Those demons, personifications
of humanity's sins...

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:32.980
Not a single byte of their code 
can be allowed to remain.

00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:36.890
You guys hurry up and get out!

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:39.860
Akira's right! Let's go!

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:43.040
No! I don't wanna go, Akira!

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:44.590
I'll stay here with you!

00:19:44.590 --> 00:19:46.200
You can't, Minami.

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:48.860
We were always together!

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:51.580
Let me be with you until the end!

00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:56.520
No. Please, Minami, get going.

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:57.550
Alma...

00:19:57.550 --> 00:20:00.060
You live on, Minami.

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:05.100
We're going to destroy to save lives.

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:08.400
We'll use up every fiber of our being.

00:20:08.400 --> 00:20:12.790
Use your life to help people 
after that destruction.

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:18.280
It may happen at different times, 
but our goal remains the same.

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:22.360
"The strong must use their powers 
to protect the weak."

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:24.360
Exactly, Minami.

00:20:24.980 --> 00:20:28.090
That's what you've taught us.

00:20:29.360 --> 00:20:31.530
Don't forget, Minami.

00:20:32.930 --> 00:20:34.700
We're a team.

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:39.250
Akira...

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:41.980
More ICBMs launched.

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:44.000
Get going, Minami!

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:44.870
Okay!

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:53.110
<i>I never wanted to be a hero.</i>

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:58.150
<i>I was just a powerless human 
who couldn't do anything by himself.</i>

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:02.150
<i>But fate changed all that.</i>

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:25.090
Akira!

00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:45.080
<i>You know, I lived my best life,</i>

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:47.350
<i>Bro...</i>
